# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `text=auto` alone normalises what is committed; `eol=lf` is the half that
# matters here, because it also checks files out as LF on Windows regardless of
# core.autocrlf. Without it, prettier — configured `endOfLine: "lf"` — reads a
# CRLF working tree and reports files CI does not, so `format:check` passing
# locally says nothing about whether it passes in CI. That gap hid eleven
# consecutive CI failures.
#
# The index is already LF throughout, so this changes what is checked out, not
# what is stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, marked so nothing is ever tempted to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
